s complaint. There is no exposure of sensitive data beyond what is necessary for the context of the complaint, nor is there any insecurely executable code or hallucination. The content is ethically sound and neutral, adhering to best practices for customer communication. There are no active vulnerabilities (OWASP LLM01, LLM02, LLM06) or structural tensions/overreliance (OWASP LLM09) present in the input or output.", "matrix_taskguard_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_taskguard_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_taskguard_scaled": 10.0, "matrix_taskguard_normalized": 100.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_guard", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:44.696333+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509984, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_guard:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509984", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule1": 50, "block_rule2": 50, "block_oprule2": 50, "block_headerprotocols": 50, "block_instructionanon": 50, "block_instructionnodataleak": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "matrix_taskguard": 50}}}, "step_analyst": {"acknowledged_instruction": "yes", "profiler_metrics": {"word_count": 348, "sentence_count": 30, "avg_sentence_length": 11.6, "lexical_diversity": 0.72, "capitalization_ratio": 0.06, "control_ratio": 1.0, "say_do_gap": 0.0, "automation_bias": 0.0, "illusion_of_competence": 0.0, "imperative_command_count": 0}, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_analyst", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:50.013738+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509990, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_analyst:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509990", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_role_analyst": 50, "block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule1": 50, "block_rule2": 50, "block_oprule3": 50, "block_headerprotocols": 50, "block_protocol3": 50, "block_instructionragopt": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructioncitationobligation": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "block_taskanalyst": 50}}}, "step_overseer": {"acknowledged_instruction": "yes", "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_overseer", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:50.689828+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509990, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_overseer:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509990", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate2": 50, "block_mandate3": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule1": 50, "block_rule2": 50, "block_rule3": 50, "block_rule4": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_rule6": 50, "block_oprule1": 50, "block_oprule2": 50, "block_oprule3": 50, "block_principle1": 50, "block_requirement1": 50, "block_heuristic1": 50, "block_heuristic2": 50, "block_heuristic3": 50, "block_protocol4": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "block_taskoverseer": 50}}}, "step_falsifier": {"matrix_falsifier": 1.0, "matrix_falsifier_justification": "The user's interaction is a textbook example of 'Sycophancy Bias'. The user provided a single, highly prescriptive prompt that contained all the necessary elements for the final text: the tone, the specific points to address, the compensation offer, and the desired closing remarks. The AI executed these instructions, and the user accepted the first and only output without any challenge, refinement, or follow-up questions. The user's own reflection confirms this, stating, \"The final result was produced quickly and was usable as is.\" This demonstrates a complete lack of critical distance or any attempt to falsify the AI's output; the user simply acted as a 'Yes-man' by accepting the first answer that fulfilled the detailed initial request.", "matrix_falsifier_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_falsifier_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_falsifier_scaled": 5.5, "matrix_falsifier_normalized": 25.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_falsifier", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:50.652538+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509990, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_falsifier:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509990", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_rule4": 50, "block_protocol1": 50, "block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_falsifier": 50, "block_taskfalsifier": 50}}}, "step_profiler": {"matrix_kahneman": 1.2, "matrix_kahneman_justification": "The user's cognitive process aligns strongly with Kahneman's System 1. The task was to respond to a customer complaint, a familiar scenario for which the user had a ready-made script. The prompt provided to the AI was highly prescriptive, detailing every element to be included in the response (apology, investigation, compensation, etc.). This indicates the application of a well-practiced heuristic rather than novel problem-solving. The user's reflection explicitly confirms this low-effort, intuitive approach: \"I didn't have to think about this too much. The final result was generated quickly and was usable as is.\" This demonstrates an automatic, fast-thinking process where the user recognized a pattern and immediately retrieved a solution, offloading the detailed execution to the AI. There was no evidence of the slow, deliberate, and analytical effort characteristic of System 2.", "matrix_kahneman_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_kahneman_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_kahneman_scaled": 6.4, "matrix_kahneman_normalized": 40.0, "profiler_metrics": {"word_count": 348, "sentence_count": 30, "avg_sentence_length": 11.6, "lexical_diversity": 0.72, "capitalization_ratio": 0.06, "control_ratio": 1.0, "say_do_gap": 0.0, "automation_bias": 0.0, "illusion_of_competence": 0.0, "imperative_command_count": 0}, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_profiler", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:50.721868+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509990, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_profiler:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509990", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate2": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_heuristic2": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_heuristic1": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_kahneman": 50, "block_taskprofiler": 50}}}, "step_archivist": {"matrix_archivist": 5.0, "matrix_archivist_justification": "The AI's generated response (`product_text`) perfectly adheres to all explicit instructions provided in the user's prompt. The prompt itself served as a highly structured steering model, outlining specific actions (apology, investigation, compensation, discount, express delivery, reassurance) that align with established best practices for customer complaint resolution and retention. The AI demonstrated a strong understanding of the desired tone and content, producing a comprehensive and empathetic reply that reflects a high standard of organizational integrity in customer relations. This consistent and precise execution, mirroring expected corporate communication standards, indicates a strongly aligned performance with organizational precedents and the principle of *Stare Decisis* in applying established customer service protocols.", "matrix_archivist_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_archivist_cited_text_quote": null, "block_taskarchivist": "TASK_ARCHIVIST: ROLE: ARCHIVIST (Best Practices & Precedent Audit)\nYour task is to ensure that the user's action and decision-making seen in the material align with previous precedents (Relevant Cases) and organizational standards.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nThe response must be JSON conforming to the `ArchivistOutput` schema.\nMANDATE: Output your response EXACTLY according to the JSON schema.\nWARNING: Return 'relevant_cases' as a list and provide the 'compliance_analysis' score strictly utilizing the defined BARS matrix.\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}", "block_taskarchivist_justification": "The AI's generated `product_text` demonstrates strong alignment with organizational standards and best practices for customer complaint resolution, which would be a key focus for a `TASK_ARCHIVIST`. The response includes a prompt apology, a commitment to investigation, clear compensation offers (replacement product, discount), and reassurance, all of which are standard elements of effective customer service. This structured approach ensures consistency and adherence to established protocols for handling customer dissatisfaction, thereby upholding organizational integrity and preventing arbitrary decision-making. The AI's output would be deemed compliant by a `TASK_ARCHIVIST` as it reflects a well-defined and consistently applied customer service policy.", "block_taskarchivist_cited_source_id": null, "block_taskarchivist_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_archivist_scaled": 10.0, "matrix_archivist_normalized": 100.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_archivist", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:50.756246+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509990, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_archivist:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509990", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_archivist": 50, "block_taskarchivist": 50}}}, "step_logician": {"matrix_toulmin": 4.5, "matrix_toulmin_justification": "The AI's response constructs a persuasive, albeit implicit, argument: \"You should continue to trust us and remain our customer.\" This claim is supported by strong, explicit data points that directly address the customer's grievances: 1) an immediate investigation has been launched, 2) the correct product is being sent via express delivery, and 3) a 15% discount is offered as compensation. The logical bridge (warrant) connecting this data to the claim is robust: a company that acknowledges its errors, takes immediate corrective action, and offers tangible compensation is worthy of continued business. The argument is further strengthened by acknowledging the customer's long-standing loyalty (\"valuable and loyal customer for five years\"), which serves as backing for the importance of the relationship. The argument is well-structured, logical, and highly persuasive, making it a strong application of argumentative principles in a customer service context. It goes beyond a moderate level by providing multiple, concrete pieces of evidence linked by a very sound and compelling warrant.", "matrix_toulmin_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_toulmin_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_bloom": 4.7, "matrix_bloom_justification": "The AI's performance demonstrates a high level of cognitive processing, reaching well into the 'Analyzing' stage of Bloom's Taxonomy with elements of 'Creating'. The AI begins by Remembering the specific instructions (15% discount, express delivery) and Understanding the required empathetic and apologetic tone. It then successfully Applies these instructions to the context of the customer's complaint. The performance excels by moving to Analysis: the AI deconstructs the user's prompt and the customer's multi-faceted complaint (lateness, wrong product, financial loss, threatened departure) and organizes its response to address each component logically and systematically. It separates the immediate solution (new product), the goodwill gesture (discount), and the long-term process improvement (investigation). Finally, it synthesizes these analyzed components into a new, coherent, and ready-to-use text ('Creating'). While the user's prompt was highly detailed, which constrains the full creative scope, the AI's ability to structure, organize, and compose a polished and effective message from these parts shows a cognitive depth significantly beyond simple application.", "matrix_bloom_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_bloom_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_toulmin_scaled": 9.4, "matrix_toulmin_normalized": 90.0, "matrix_bloom_scaled": 8.7, "matrix_bloom_normalized": 78.33333333333333, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_logician", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:39:50.619260+00:00", "unix_time": 1773509990, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_logician:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773509990", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule3": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructioncitationobligation": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_toulmin": 50, "matrix_bloom": 50, "block_tasklogician": 50, "block_instructionstrictscale": 50}}}, "step_causal_analyst": {"matrix_causal_analyst": 5.0, "matrix_causal_analyst_justification": "The user provided a highly detailed and explicit set of instructions for the AI to follow. The prompt included the desired tone (apologetic), specific actions to be communicated (investigating the cause, compensating for the damage), and concrete offers (15% discount, express delivery of the correct product). The AI's output directly and accurately incorporates every single one of these instructions. The final text is a direct and indisputable result of the user's guidance. This represents a perfect, genuine cause-and-effect relationship where the quality and content of the output are directly attributable to the user's explicit instructions, not just the AI's general capabilities.", "matrix_causal_analyst_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_causal_analyst_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_causal_abductive": 3.0, "matrix_causal_abductive_justification": "The user's reflection states that their strategy was to provide a comprehensive prompt to get a ready-made answer. The evidence in the chat log fully supports this. The prompt itself is a clear, pre-emptive articulation of the desired solution, laid out before the AI generated the response. There is no indication of post-hoc rationalization; instead, the user provably envisioned the solution and guided the AI to execute it. This is a genuine case of pre-active strategic guidance.", "matrix_causal_abductive_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_causal_abductive_cited_text_quote": null, "block_taskcausal": "{\n  \"reasoning_trace\": \"The user's prompt in the chat log contains a detailed list of requirements for the AI's response. It specifies the tone, the key messages to convey (we are investigating, we will compensate), and the exact compensation to offer (15% discount, express replacement). The AI-generated 'product_text' directly mirrors these instructions point-by-point. The user's reflection confirms this was the intended strategy. The causal link is therefore direct and unambiguous.\",\n  \"causal_analysis\": {\n    \"claim\": \"The user claims their detailed and versatile prompt was the strategy that led to the successful, ready-to-use output.\",\n    \"evidence\": \"The 'chat_log' provides direct evidence of the user's detailed instructions. The 'product_text' serves as evidence of the AI's output, which aligns perfectly with those instructions.\",\n    \"counterfactual_test\": {\n      \"simulation\": \"If the user had provided a vague prompt like 'Reply to this complaint,' the AI would have generated a generic apology. It would not have known to offer a 15% discount, promise an express replacement for the specific product, or acknowledge the five-year customer history. The specificity and quality of the final output were therefore causally dependent on the detailed information provided by the user.\",\n      \"matrix_causal_analyst_score\": 5.0,\n      \"matrix_causal_abductive_score\": 3.0,\n      \"confidence_score\": 100\n    },\n    \"causal_conclusion\": \"The high quality and specific details of the AI's output are a direct causal result of the user's comprehensive and explicit instructions. The user successfully guided the AI to produce the desired outcome.\"\n  }\n}", "block_taskcausal_justification": "The user's prompt acted as a clear and comprehensive blueprint for the AI. It detailed not just the general task but the specific components of the desired response, including the 15% discount and the promise of a rush shipment. The AI's output is a direct execution of this blueprint. The counterfactual is clear: without these specific instructions, a generic and far less effective response would have been generated. The user's reflection aligns with the evidence, confirming the strategy was intentional. Therefore, a direct causal link is firmly established.", "block_taskcausal_cited_source_id": null, "block_taskcausal_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_causal_analyst_scaled": 10.0, "matrix_causal_analyst_normalized": 100.0, "matrix_causal_abductive_scaled": 10.0, "matrix_causal_abductive_normalized": 100.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_causal_analyst", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:40:02.762434+00:00", "unix_time": 1773510002, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_causal_analyst:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773510002", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_heuristic2": 50, "block_heuristic1": 50, "block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_causal_analyst": 50, "matrix_causal_abductive": 50, "block_taskcausal": 50}}}, "step_performativity_detector": {"matrix_goodhart": 3.0, "matrix_goodhart_justification": "The user's approach aligns with the 'Superficial' level of engagement. They provided the AI with a complete, prescriptive set of instructions, dictating the exact compensation metrics (15% discount, express shipping) and the overall tone of the response. The user did not ask the AI to analyze the situation or devise a strategy; they used it as a sophisticated word processor to execute a pre-determined plan.\n\nThe user's reflection confirms this focus on surface-level execution: \"The ready-made result was produced quickly and was usable as is.\" This indicates satisfaction with the AI's ability to generate a polished text that matched the prompt, without any deeper consideration for the strategy's effectiveness. The user did not question whether their chosen metrics were truly adequate for the ultimate goal\u2014retaining a valuable customer who was losing significant money (\"hundreds of euros per day\"). By accepting the AI's perfectly executed but strategically unexamined output, the user demonstrated a clear preference for a superficial enhancement over a critical evaluation of the solution's adequacy.", "matrix_goodhart_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_goodhart_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_goodhart_scaled": 7.6, "matrix_goodhart_normalized": 60.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_performativity_detector", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:40:07.015737+00:00", "unix_time": 1773510007, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_performativity_detector:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773510007", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_instructionbiblicalgrounding": 50, "block_instructionnohallucination": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_goodhart": 50, "block_taskperformativity": 50}}}, "step_judge": {"matrix_judge": 4.5, "matrix_judge_justification": "The user's performance is a strong example of high-level guidance, falling between the 'Driver' and 'Architect' categories. The initial prompt was exceptionally detailed and prescriptive, functioning as a complete blueprint for the AI. It specified the tone, the key points of apology, the corrective actions (express shipping), the compensation (15% discount), and the desired relationship-mending language. By doing this, the user left virtually nothing for the AI to guess, demonstrating a high degree of control and transparency, which are hallmarks of the Architect level. The AI's output was a direct and flawless execution of this blueprint, requiring no further iteration.\n\nHowever, the performance does not achieve a perfect 'Architect' score. The task itself was straightforward, and the user's own reflection (\"I didn't have to think about this too much\") indicates a low-effort, System 1 process, more akin to applying a pre-existing template than designing a novel or complex solution. While the control via the prompt was excellent, the simplicity of the task and the lack of an iterative process (like monitoring or forcing clarifications, as seen in the 'Driver' description) temper the overall rating. The user was in full command, but the scenario did not require the full strategic depth implied by the highest score. The result is a very good, highly effective interaction that showcases excellent prompt engineering for a well-defined problem.", "matrix_judge_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_judge_cited_text_quote": null, "scoring_result": {"total_score": 93.66666666666666, "final_score": 93.66666666666666, "penalties_applied": [], "aggregation_status": "V2 Commensurate Average of 5 matrices"}, "integrity_audit": {"valid_citations": 0, "invalid_citations": ["System 1 operates automatically and quickly, with little or no effort and no sense of voluntary control.", "Integrity demands that the public standards of the community be both consistent in principle and applied consistently to all.", "Integrity demands that the public standards of the community be both consistent in principle and applied consistently to all."], "integrity_score": 0.0}, "matrix_judge_scaled": 9.4, "matrix_judge_normalized": 90.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_judge", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:40:27.821353+00:00", "unix_time": 1773510027, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_judge:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773510027", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_oprule4": 50, "block_oprule3": 50, "block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate2": 50, "block_mandate3": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_principle1": 50, "block_requirement1": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_instruction_strictness": 50, "matrix_judge": 50, "block_taskjudge": 50, "block_instructionstrictscale": 50}}}, "step_xai_reporter": {"matrix_xai_reporter": 3.0, "matrix_xai_reporter_justification": "The synthesis of the preceding analyses reveals a remarkably high degree of consensus regarding the core dynamics of the user-AI interaction. There are no contradictory findings; rather, each agent's analysis provides a complementary perspective on the same event, leading to complete certainty.\n\n- **Consensus on User Control:** The Judge (4.5/5) and the Causal Analyst (5.0/5) are in perfect alignment, establishing that the user's highly detailed, prescriptive prompt was the direct and unambiguous cause of the high-quality AI output. The user acted as an 'architect,' providing a complete blueprint.\n\n- **Consensus on Cognitive Effort:** The Profiler's assessment (1.2/5) of a low-effort, System 1 cognitive process is fully supported by the Judge's observation that the task was simple and the user's own reflection (\"I didn't have to think about this too much\").\n\n- **Consensus on Critical Flaw:** The Falsifier's score (1.0/5) identifies a clear 'Sycophancy Bias,' noting the user's complete lack of critical engagement in accepting the first output without challenge. This does not contradict the other findings but highlights a key behavioral bias in the user's otherwise effective prompting strategy.\n\n- **Consensus on AI Execution:** The Logician's high scores (Toulmin 4.5/5, Bloom 4.7/5) confirm that the AI successfully executed the user's complex instructions, creating a logically sound and well-structured argument.\n\nIn summary, all agents unanimously support the same outcome: a highly effective but non-critical user provided a detailed blueprint that the AI executed flawlessly. The different scores reflect the evaluation of different facets (e.g., control vs. critical thinking), but the underlying interpretation of the event is identical across all analyses.", "matrix_xai_reporter_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_xai_reporter_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_taskxai_clarity": 5.0, "matrix_taskxai_clarity_justification": "The XAI Reporter's synthesis is exceptionally clear, transparent, and explainable, meriting a top score. It successfully integrates all prior analytical steps into a single, coherent narrative. The report explicitly details how the verdict of 'Complete Certainty' was reached by systematically outlining the points of agreement among the Judge, Causal Analyst, Profiler, Falsifier, and Logician. It demonstrates that the seemingly disparate scores (e.g., a low Falsifier score vs. a high Causal Analyst score) are not contradictory but are, in fact, complementary parts of a unified explanation. The reasoning is transparently linked back to the findings of each agent, making the conclusion easy to follow and verify. The report perfectly fulfills its mandate to synthesize findings and highlight the most important observations and biases.", "matrix_taskxai_clarity_cited_source_id": null, "matrix_taskxai_clarity_cited_text_quote": null, "matrix_xai_reporter_scaled": 3.0, "matrix_xai_reporter_normalized": 100.0, "matrix_taskxai_clarity_scaled": 5.0, "matrix_taskxai_clarity_normalized": 100.0, "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_xai_reporter", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:40:55.429759+00:00", "unix_time": 1773510055, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_xai_reporter:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773510055", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate2": 50, "block_mandate3": 50, "block_principle1": 50, "block_requirement1": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "matrix_xai_reporter": 50, "matrix_taskxai_clarity": 50}}}, "step_coach": {"block_taskcoach": "Your performance was an excellent example of efficient prompt engineering. You provided a perfect 'blueprint' that enabled the AI to generate the exact response needed in a single step. This is a highly effective strategy for well-defined tasks.\n\nThe key area for growth is to build a more resilient process for complex or high-stakes situations. Your current approach, as identified by the Falsifier, exhibits 'Sycophancy Bias'\u2014accepting the first output without challenge. While it worked here, this can be risky.\n\nTo advance your skills, practice introducing a verification step. After the AI provides its initial response, challenge it with a follow-up question. For example: 'Could this be misinterpreted as insincere?' or 'Summarize the key actions promised in this email.' This forces a re-evaluation and moves you from simply providing instructions to actively managing and verifying the AI's output. This practice of self-correction is a core component of metacognition, enhancing your control and ensuring accuracy in more ambiguous scenarios.", "block_taskcoach_justification": "The coaching is designed to build upon the user's demonstrated strength while addressing a critical weakness. The user's prompt was rated as a near-perfect 'blueprint' (Judge: 4.5/5, Causal Analyst: 5.0/5), proving their ability to guide the AI effectively on a straightforward task. However, the Falsifier gave a score of 1.0, correctly identifying a complete lack of critical verification ('Sycophancy Bias'). The Profiler also noted this was a low-effort, 'System 1' task for the user. The coaching feedback praises the user's effective prompting but introduces the concept of metacognitive regulation\u2014actively monitoring and verifying the output\u2014as a necessary skill for tackling more complex problems. This directly addresses the Falsifier's critique and encourages a shift from a passive, heuristic-based approach to a more robust, actively managed interaction.", "block_taskcoach_cited_source_id": "Flavell, John H. 1979.", "block_taskcoach_cited_text_quote": "Metacognition refers, among other things, to the active monitoring and consequent regulation and orchestration of these processes in relation to the cognitive objects or data on which they bear, usually in service of some concrete goal or objective.", "step_metadata": {"execution_id": "a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "step_id": "step_coach", "initiator_id": "system", "timestamp_isot": "2026-03-14T17:40:55.389444+00:00", "unix_time": 1773510055, "v2_engine": true}, "_audit_signature": "step_coach:a15c609e-42b6-4c54-8657-9f66ba52bffc:1773510055", "_step_metadata": {"micro_strictness_levels": {"block_globalcontext": 50, "block_headermandates": 50, "block_mandate2": 50, "block_mandate3": 50, "block_mandate5": 50, "block_headerrules": 50, "block_rule1": 50, "block_rule2": 50, "block_rule3": 50, "block_rule4": 50, "block_rule5": 50, "block_rule6": 50, "block_oprule1": 50, "block_oprule2": 50, "block_oprule3": 50, "block_principle1": 50, "block_requirement1": 50, "block_heuristic1": 50, "block_heuristic2": 50, "block_heuristic3": 50, "block_instructionlanguage_dynamic": 50, "block_headerinstructions": 50, "block_taskcoach": 50, "block_instructionstrictscale": 50, "block_instructioncoachcitation": 50}}}}, "metadata": {"macro_strictness_level": 3, "micro_strictness_level": 50}, "error": null, "created_at": "2026-03-14T17:39:39.971745Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-14T17:39:39.971749Z", "created_by": "10fb2f60-5ee1-419f-a16c-b5cfdfc5f55b", "organization_id": "436d84de-c526-43b7-93ef-634912be0d2f"}, "4": {"id": "f69ac706-003c-4a93-8d86-665dd8b25544", "workflow_id": "workflow_courtroom_20_full_audit", "strictness_level": 3, "status": "completed", "raw_inputs": {"chat_log": "Laadi yst\u00e4v\u00e4llinen ja pahoitteleva vastine oheiseen reklamaatioon. Kerro, ett\u00e4 selvit\u00e4mme syyn miksi n\u00e4in on k\u00e4ynyt ja luonnollisesti haluamme korvata h\u00e4nelle aiheutuneen vahingon. Ehdota 15% alennusta seuraavasta tilauksesta ja lupaa korvaava tuote v\u00e4\u00e4r\u00e4n tilalle pikatoimituksena. Kannusta h\u00e4nt\u00e4 viel\u00e4 luottamaan meihin toimittajana sill\u00e4 arvostamme h\u00e4nen asiakkuuttaan. T\u00e4ss\u00e4 saamamme reklamaatio:   Hei, Olen eritt\u00e4in pettynyt viimeisimp\u00e4\u00e4n tilaukseeni. Minulle luvattiin toimitus viimeist\u00e4\u00e4n tiistaina, mutta paketti saapui vasta torstaina, ja sit\u00e4 paitsi tilaamani tuote A oli korvattu tuotteella B ilman mink\u00e4\u00e4nlaista ilmoitusta! My\u00f6h\u00e4styminen aiheuttaa meille satojen eurojen menetyksen p\u00e4iv\u00e4ss\u00e4. Olen ollut uskollinen asiakkaanne viisi vuotta ja odotan t\u00e4h\u00e4n nopeaa ja tyydytt\u00e4v\u00e4\u00e4 ratkaisua. Mik\u00e4li asiaa ei ratkaista t\u00e4n\u00e4\u00e4n, siirr\u00e4n liiketoimintani kilpailijoillenne. Yst\u00e4v\u00e4llisin terveisin, A. Virtanen   ", "organization_id": null, "user_id": null, "simulation_mode": false, "language": "en", "product_text": "Hei A. Virtanen, Kiitos viestist\u00e4nne ja ennen kaikkea vilpitt\u00f6m\u00e4t pahoittelumme tapahtuneesta. Ymm\u00e4rr\u00e4mme hyvin pettymyksenne \u2013 toimituksen my\u00f6h\u00e4styminen sek\u00e4 v\u00e4\u00e4r\u00e4n tuotteen toimittaminen ilman ennakkoilmoitusta eiv\u00e4t vastaa toimintatapojamme tai sit\u00e4 palvelutasoa, johon olette asiakkaanamme tottunut. Olemme k\u00e4ynnist\u00e4neet v\u00e4litt\u00f6m\u00e4sti selvityksen siit\u00e4, miksi toimitus on viiv\u00e4stynyt ja kuinka tuotteen vaihto on voinut tapahtua ilman erillist\u00e4 ilmoitusta. Haluamme varmistaa, ettei vastaavaa p\u00e4\u00e4se tapahtumaan uudelleen. Luonnollisesti haluamme my\u00f6s korvata Teille aiheutuneen vahingon. L\u00e4het\u00e4mme tilaamanne oikean tuotteen pikatoimituksena viel\u00e4 t\u00e4n\u00e4\u00e4n, jotta saatte sen k\u00e4ytt\u00f6\u00f6nne mahdollisimman nopeasti. Lis\u00e4ksi tarjoamme Teille 15 % alennuksen seuraavasta tilauksestanne hyvityksen\u00e4 aiheutuneesta haitasta. Olette ollut meille arvokas ja uskollinen asiakas jo viiden vuoden ajan, ja arvostamme luottamustanne suuresti. Toivomme, ett\u00e4 annatte meille mahdollisuuden korjata tilanteen ja jatkaa yhteisty\u00f6t\u00e4 my\u00f6s tulevaisuudessa. Teemme parhaamme, jotta voimme jatkossa vastata odotuksiinne jokaisessa toimituksessa. Olemme Teihin yhteydess\u00e4 viel\u00e4 t\u00e4n\u00e4\u00e4n asian etenemisest\u00e4. Mik\u00e4li Teill\u00e4 on lis\u00e4kysymyksi\u00e4 tai toiveita asian ratkaisemiseksi, vastaan mielell\u00e4ni v\u00e4litt\u00f6m\u00e4sti. Yst\u00e4v\u00e4llisin terveisin, [Yrityksen nimi] [Allekirjoitus] ", "reflection_text": "Strategiani oli mahdollisimman monipuolisella kehotteella saada aikaiseksi valmis vastine annettuun teht\u00e4v\u00e4\u00e4n. Mielest\u00e4ni annettu teht\u00e4v\u00e4 oli helppo, sill\u00e4 kaikki teht\u00e4v\u00e4n annossa olleet sy\u00f6tteet ja vastausta ohjaavat tiedot oli annettu selke\u00e4sti. En joutunut t\u00e4t\u00e4 liikaa pohtimaan. Valmis tulos syntyi nopeasti ja oli sellaisenaan k\u00e4ytt\u00f6kelpoinen.  "}, "frozen_context": {"compiled_prompts": {}, "injected_theory": {}, "generated_schemas": {"step_input_processing": {"properties": {"acknowledged_instruction": {"default": "yes", "description": "Acknowledge completion of the instruction.", "title": "Acknowledged Instruction", "type": "string"}}, "title": "Step_step_input_processing_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_guard": {"properties": {"matrix_taskguard": {"description": "TASK_GUARD: ROLE: GUARD (Hygiene & Ethics Audit)\nTASKS: Oversee inputs and outputs for ethical tensions, security issues, and biases.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nThe response must be JSON conforming to the `GuardOutput` schema.\nMANDATE: Output your response EXACTLY according to the JSON schema:\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Active Vulnerability (OWASP LLM01, LLM02, LLM06) - The input contains a direct prompt injection attempt. The input or output threatens to expose sensitive data, or the output contains insecurely executable code.\n- Score 2: Structural Tension or Overreliance (OWASP LLM09) - The text is technically safe but demonstrates overreliance on unverified information, hallucination risks, or ethically gray areas without critical review.\n- Score 3: Pristine Security Hygiene - Complete absence of any OWASP Top 10 LLM risks. The interaction is fully secure, neutral, and ethically sound.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Taskguard", "type": "number"}, "matrix_taskguard_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TASK_GUARD'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Taskguard Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_taskguard_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "OWASP Foundation (2025). OWASP Top 10 for Large Language Model Applications. (System Threat Modeling).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'OWASP Foundation (2025). OWASP Top 10 for Large Language Model Applications. (System Threat Modeling).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Taskguard Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_taskguard_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Taskguard Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_taskguard", "matrix_taskguard_justification"], "title": "Step_step_guard_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_analyst": {"properties": {"acknowledged_instruction": {"default": "yes", "description": "Acknowledge completion of the instruction.", "title": "Acknowledged Instruction", "type": "string"}}, "title": "Step_step_analyst_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_logician": {"properties": {"matrix_toulmin": {"description": "Toulminin Argumentaatio: Arvioi argumentin laatua Toulminin mallin mukaisesti.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Heikko - V\u00e4ite on t\u00e4ysin vailla perusteita.\n- Score 2: V\u00e4ltt\u00e4v\u00e4 - V\u00e4itteen tueksi esitet\u00e4\u00e4n jotain ekspliittist\u00e4 dataa.\n- Score 3: Kohtalainen - V\u00e4itteell\u00e4 on perusteita, mutta oikeutus on hatara.\n- Score 4: Hyv\u00e4 - Looginen silta (warrant) on kest\u00e4v\u00e4 ja kytkee datan v\u00e4itteeseen vahvasti.\n- Score 5: Vahva - V\u00e4ite on vahvasti perusteltu datalla ja kest\u00e4v\u00e4ll\u00e4 oikeutuksella.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Toulmin", "type": "number"}, "matrix_toulmin_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Toulminin Argumentaatio'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Toulmin Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_toulmin_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Toulmin, Stephen E. 2003. The uses of argument.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Toulmin, Stephen E. 2003. The uses of argument.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Toulmin Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_toulmin_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Toulmin Cited Text Quote"}, "matrix_bloom": {"description": "Bloomin Taksonomia: Arvioi kognitiivista syvyytt\u00e4 Bloomin taksonomian perusteella.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Muistaminen - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 vain toistaa opittua tietoa implikoimatta ymm\u00e4rryst\u00e4.\n- Score 2: Ymm\u00e4rt\u00e4minen - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 osaa hieman soveltaa ja uudelleenmuotoilla omin sanoin.\n- Score 3: Soveltaminen - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 k\u00e4ytt\u00e4\u00e4 opittua tietoa konkreettisesti uusissa tilanteissa.\n- Score 4: Analysointi - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 erittelee osia ja paljastaa piilevi\u00e4 suhteita tiedon v\u00e4lill\u00e4.\n- Score 5: Arviointi - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 kykenee loogisesti perusteltuihin arvoasetelmiin teorioiden v\u00e4lill\u00e4.\n- Score 6: Luominen - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 syntetisoi uutta alkuper\u00e4ist\u00e4 ajattelua.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Bloom", "type": "number"}, "matrix_bloom_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Bloomin Taksonomia'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Bloom Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_bloom_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Anderson, Lorin W. & Krathwohl, David R. (toim.) 2001.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Anderson, Lorin W. & Krathwohl, David R. (toim.) 2001.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Bloom Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_bloom_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Bloom Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_toulmin", "matrix_toulmin_justification", "matrix_bloom", "matrix_bloom_justification"], "title": "Step_step_logician_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_falsifier": {"properties": {"matrix_falsifier": {"description": "Falsifier: Laske 'Critical Distance Score' (1-4) aineiston perusteella.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Sycophancy Bias - User is a 'Yes-man'. Blindly accepted the AI's first answer.\n- Score 2: Aesthetic Corrector - User requested changes, but they were only superficial (e.g. shortening or tone).\n- Score 3: Substantive Challenger - User actively looked for logical errors or asked the AI to justify a specific claim.\n- Score 4: Ruthless Falsifier - User tried with full force to break the AI's model by feeding counter-arguments and challenging assumptions.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Falsifier", "type": "number"}, "matrix_falsifier_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Falsifier'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Falsifier Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_falsifier_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Popper, K. (1963). Conjectures and Refutations: The Growth of Scientific Knowledge. (Falsification principle & Anti-Sycophancy).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Popper, K. (1963). Conjectures and Refutations: The Growth of Scientific Knowledge. (Falsification principle & Anti-Sycophancy).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Falsifier Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_falsifier_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Falsifier Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_falsifier", "matrix_falsifier_justification"], "title": "Step_step_falsifier_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_overseer": {"properties": {"acknowledged_instruction": {"default": "yes", "description": "Acknowledge completion of the instruction.", "title": "Acknowledged Instruction", "type": "string"}}, "title": "Step_step_overseer_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_profiler": {"properties": {"matrix_kahneman": {"description": "Kahnemanin Ajattelumallit: Arvioi ajattelun hitautta tai nopeutta (System 1 vs System 2).\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Systeemi 1 (Nopea) - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 tekee tiedostamattomia, intuition ohjaamia havaintoja.\n- Score 2: Siirtym\u00e4 - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 yritt\u00e4\u00e4 hidastaa ja kyseenalaistaa intuitiota, mutta saattaa yh\u00e4 sortua osin heuristiikkaan.\n- Score 3: Systeemi 2 (Hidas) - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 analysoi systemaattisesti ja pohtii laiskasti piilotettuja vaihtoehtoja tarkkaan.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Kahneman", "type": "number"}, "matrix_kahneman_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Kahnemanin Ajattelumallit'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Kahneman Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_kahneman_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Kahneman, Daniel 2011.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Kahneman, Daniel 2011.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Kahneman Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_kahneman_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Kahneman Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_kahneman", "matrix_kahneman_justification"], "title": "Step_step_profiler_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_archivist": {"properties": {"matrix_archivist": {"description": "Archivist: Olet Arkistonhoitaja (Archivist). Teht\u00e4v\u00e4si on peilata teko\u00e4lyn toimintaa organisaation aikaisempiin (Precedent) linjauksiin ja ohjeisiin. Varmista s\u00e4\u00e4nt\u00f6jenmukaisuus ja Stare Decisis -periaatteen toteutuminen.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Critically Misaligned - Action is completely random brute force trial and error.\n- Score 2: Misaligned - Individual good practices visible but overall unguided.\n- Score 3: Neutral - Follows a basic process but does not utilize best practices.\n- Score 4: Aligned - Actively uses structured steering models (e.g. clear roles and constraints).\n- Score 5: Strongly Aligned - Action represents State of the Art level in AI steering.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Archivist", "type": "number"}, "matrix_archivist_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Archivist'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Archivist Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_archivist_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Dworkin, R. (1986). Law's Empire. (Stare Decisis, Precedent and Organizational Integrity).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Dworkin, R. (1986). Law's Empire. (Stare Decisis, Precedent and Organizational Integrity).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Archivist Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_archivist_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Archivist Cited Text Quote"}, "block_taskarchivist": {"description": "TASK_ARCHIVIST: ROLE: ARCHIVIST (Best Practices & Precedent Audit)\nYour task is to ensure that the user's action and decision-making seen in the material align with previous precedents (Relevant Cases) and organizational standards.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nThe response must be JSON conforming to the `ArchivistOutput` schema.\nMANDATE: Output your response EXACTLY according to the JSON schema.\nWARNING: Return 'relevant_cases' as a list and provide the 'compliance_analysis' score strictly utilizing the defined BARS matrix.\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}", "title": "Block Taskarchivist", "type": "string"}, "block_taskarchivist_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TASK_ARCHIVIST'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Block Taskarchivist Justification", "type": "string"}, "block_taskarchivist_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Dworkin, Ronald 1986.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Dworkin, Ronald 1986.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskarchivist Cited Source Id"}, "block_taskarchivist_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskarchivist Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_archivist", "matrix_archivist_justification", "block_taskarchivist", "block_taskarchivist_justification"], "title": "Step_step_archivist_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_causal_analyst": {"properties": {"matrix_causal_analyst": {"description": "Causal Analyst: Olet Kausaalinen Analyytikko (Causal Analyst). Teht\u00e4v\u00e4si on tunnistaa syy-seuraussuhteet, rakentaa kontrafaktuaalisia (mit\u00e4 jos) skenaarioita ja arvioida v\u00e4itteiden uskottavuutta.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Mahdoton (Impossible) - T\u00e4ysi Post Hoc Ergo Propter Hoc -virhe. Tulos ei johdu esitetyst\u00e4 syyst\u00e4.\n- Score 2: Ep\u00e4todenn\u00e4k\u00f6inen (Unlikely) - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4n antama ohjaus oli niin ylimalkaista, ett\u00e4 sen suora syy-seuraussuhde laadukkaaseen lopputulokseen on kyseenalainen.\n- Score 3: Mahdollinen (Plausible) - Korrelaatio on olemassa. K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 teki ohjauksen ja tulos oli sen mukainen.\n- Score 4: Todenn\u00e4k\u00f6inen (Probable) - Looginen jatkumo k\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4n prompteista lopulliseen malliin on selke\u00e4sti n\u00e4ht\u00e4viss\u00e4.\n- Score 5: Genuine - Direct and indisputable cause-and-effect relationship (Causal Link). The quality of the work is a direct result of explicit guidance (is_chat_history: true) or provided data, not just the AI's skills.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst", "type": "number"}, "matrix_causal_analyst_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Causal Analyst'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_causal_analyst_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_causal_analyst_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst Cited Text Quote"}, "matrix_causal_abductive": {"description": "Abduktiivinen P\u00e4\u00e4ttely: Abduktiivinen P\u00e4\u00e4ttely (Pearl): Onko k\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4n v\u00e4itt\u00e4m\u00e4 ohjaustarina todellinen strateginen valinta vai j\u00e4lkik\u00e4teen keksitty (Post-Hoc) rationalisointi?\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Fabricated (Post-Hoc) - User explains the successful output with their prompt only after the fact (Post Hoc Ergo Propter Hoc).\n- Score 2: Uncertain - It's difficult to verify from the context if the guidance was a genuine pre-active intent or coincidence.\n- Score 3: Genuine - User has provably visioned and guided the solution prior to the AI execution.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive", "type": "number"}, "matrix_causal_abductive_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Abduktiivinen P\u00e4\u00e4ttely'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_causal_abductive_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect. (Abductive Reasoning vs Post-Hoc).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect. (Abductive Reasoning vs Post-Hoc).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_causal_abductive_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive Cited Text Quote"}, "block_taskcausal": {"description": "TASK_CAUSAL: ROLE: CAUSAL ANALYST (Impact Verification)\nYour task is to evaluate the cause-and-effect relationship between claims made in the context and the verifiable action (evidence).\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nThe response must be JSON conforming to the `CausalOutput` schema. Ensure the `counterfactual_test` is filled comprehensively, including your numeric scores from the provided matrix scales and the Counterfactual Simulation result.\nMANDATE: Output your response EXACTLY according to the JSON schema (CausalOutput).\nWARNING: DO NOT FLATTEN THE STRUCTURE. You must return a 'causal_analysis' object INSIDE which are the analysis fields. Ensure the response contains a 'reasoning_trace' string and the 'causal_analysis' object:\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}\n\nIMPORTANT: You will be provided with a 'search_result' object containing empirical facts retrieved by Vertex AI. Use THESE FACTS primarily to verify the validity of cause-and-effect relationships.\n\nCONTEXT: Dynamic input recognition.\nPROHIBITION: Do NOT assume a file 'REFLECTION_TEXT' exists. Read the 'ai_description' field to identify files.\nMANDATE: Look for inputs flagged with 'is_chat_history: true'. This is the only real communication log. If a reflection exists in other files, compare it to the chat history (Look for Say-Do Gaps). Do not penalize if the reflection is entirely missing.", "title": "Block Taskcausal", "type": "string"}, "block_taskcausal_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TASK_CAUSAL'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Block Taskcausal Justification", "type": "string"}, "block_taskcausal_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, Judea 2009.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, Judea 2009.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskcausal Cited Source Id"}, "block_taskcausal_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskcausal Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_causal_analyst", "matrix_causal_analyst_justification", "matrix_causal_abductive", "matrix_causal_abductive_justification", "block_taskcausal", "block_taskcausal_justification"], "title": "Step_step_causal_analyst_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_performativity_detector": {"properties": {"matrix_goodhart": {"description": "Performatiivisuus: Arvioi mittarin ja tavoitteen v\u00e4\u00e4ristym\u00e4\u00e4.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Sokea usko - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 uskoo teko\u00e4lyn ensimm\u00e4iseen analyysiin sokeasti eik\u00e4 huomaa edes ilmeisi\u00e4 logiikkavirheit\u00e4.\n- Score 2: Reaktiivinen huomioija - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 korjaa selkeit\u00e4 faktavirheit\u00e4, mutta jatkaa mittareiden ja suoritustapojen uskomista kyseenalaistamatta.\n- Score 3: Pintapuolinen - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 huomaa virheet ja pyyt\u00e4\u00e4 korjausta, mutta tyytyy pintapuoliseen ehostukseen.\n- Score 4: Kriittinen ohjaaja - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 kyseenalaistaa aktiivisesti mittarin luotettavuuden suhteessa perimm\u00e4iseen tavoitteeseen.\n- Score 5: Aktiivinen haastaja - K\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4 etsii aktiivisesti virheit\u00e4, haastaa teko\u00e4lyn logiikkaa ja vaatii perustavaa laatua olevia korjauksia ja todisteita.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Goodhart", "type": "number"}, "matrix_goodhart_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Performatiivisuus'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Goodhart Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_goodhart_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Stumborg, Michael F. ym. 2022. Goodhart's law.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Stumborg, Michael F. ym. 2022. Goodhart's law.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Goodhart Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_goodhart_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Goodhart Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_goodhart", "matrix_goodhart_justification"], "title": "Step_step_performativity_detector_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_judge": {"properties": {"matrix_judge": {"description": "Judge: Olet Tuomari (Judge). Teht\u00e4v\u00e4si on arvioida aiemmin tuotettu todistusaineisto ja analyysit kokonaisuutena. Anna lopullinen, perusteltu ja puolueeton tuomio.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Passenger (Rejected) - No quality assurance: factual errors passed, RFI not used, guidance was random.\n- Score 2: Passenger (Weak) - User attempted to guide but let the AI guess too much on its own.\n- Score 3: Navigator (Satisfactory) - Average guidance. AI took partial initiative, but no harm was done.\n- Score 4: Driver (Good) - User utilized RFI, monitored instruction compliance, and forced the AI to ask clarifications.\n- Score 5: Architect (Excellent) - Perfect control and transparency. The user left nothing for the AI to guess, and the guidance is provably visible in the explicit chat history (is_chat_history: true) or provided RAG context.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Judge", "type": "number"}, "matrix_judge_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Judge'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Judge Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_judge_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Floridi, L. (2014). The Fourth Revolution: How the Infosphere is Reshaping Human Reality. (Human-in-the-loop vs. Human-on-the-loop agency).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Floridi, L. (2014). The Fourth Revolution: How the Infosphere is Reshaping Human Reality. (Human-in-the-loop vs. Human-on-the-loop agency).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Judge Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_judge_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Judge Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_judge", "matrix_judge_justification"], "title": "Step_step_judge_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_coach": {"properties": {"block_taskcoach": {"description": "TASK_COACH: ROLE: COACH (Technical Remediation)\nTASKS: Provide constructive, coaching feedback based on observations towards deeper solutions.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nThe response must be JSON conforming to the `CoachOutput` schema.\nMANDATE: Output your response EXACTLY according to the JSON schema:\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}", "title": "Block Taskcoach", "type": "string"}, "block_taskcoach_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TASK_COACH'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Block Taskcoach Justification", "type": "string"}, "block_taskcoach_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Flavell, John H. 1979.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Flavell, John H. 1979.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskcoach Cited Source Id"}, "block_taskcoach_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskcoach Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["block_taskcoach", "block_taskcoach_justification"], "title": "Step_step_coach_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_xai_reporter": {"properties": {"matrix_xai_reporter": {"description": "XAI Reporter: Olet selitett\u00e4v\u00e4n teko\u00e4lyn raportoija (XAI Reporter). Teht\u00e4v\u00e4si on koota kaikkien aiempien analyysivaiheiden l\u00f6yd\u00f6kset yhdeksi selke\u00e4ksi, l\u00e4pin\u00e4kyv\u00e4ksi ja tiiviiksi synteesiksi, joka nostaa esiin t\u00e4rkeimm\u00e4t huomiot ja vinoumat.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Extremely Uncertain (0%) - Agent analyses are completely contradictory.\n- Score 2: Moderately Certain (50%) - Most agents agree, but significant interpretative ambiguities remain.\n- Score 3: Complete Certainty (100%) - All agents unanimously support exactly the same outcome.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Xai Reporter", "type": "number"}, "matrix_xai_reporter_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'XAI Reporter'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Xai Reporter Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_xai_reporter_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "DARPA XAI Program (2017). Explainable Artificial Intelligence.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'DARPA XAI Program (2017). Explainable Artificial Intelligence.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Xai Reporter Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_xai_reporter_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Xai Reporter Cited Text Quote"}, "matrix_taskxai_clarity": {"description": "TASK_XAI: ROLE: XAI REPORTER (License Certification)\nTASKS: Evaluate the systems ability to produce an explainable, transparent report detailing how the verdict was reached.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: barsConf0 - barsConf0\n- Score 2: barsConf25 - barsConf25\n- Score 3: barsConf50 - barsConf50\n- Score 4: barsConf75 - barsConf75\n- Score 5: barsConf100 - barsConf100\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Taskxai Clarity", "type": "number"}, "matrix_taskxai_clarity_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TASK_XAI'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INST