hat_history: true) or provided data, not just the AI's skills.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst", "type": "number"}, "matrix_causal_analyst_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Causal Analyst'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_causal_analyst_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_causal_analyst_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Analyst Cited Text Quote"}, "matrix_causal_abductive": {"description": "Abduktiivinen P\u00e4\u00e4ttely: Abduktiivinen P\u00e4\u00e4ttely (Pearl): Onko k\u00e4ytt\u00e4j\u00e4n v\u00e4itt\u00e4m\u00e4 ohjaustarina todellinen strateginen valinta vai j\u00e4lkik\u00e4teen keksitty (Post-Hoc) rationalisointi?\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Fabricated (Post-Hoc) - User explains the successful output with their prompt only after the fact (Post Hoc Ergo Propter Hoc).\n- Score 2: Uncertain - It's difficult to verify from the context if the guidance was a genuine pre-active intent or coincidence.\n- Score 3: Genuine - User has provably visioned and guided the solution prior to the AI execution.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive", "type": "number"}, "matrix_causal_abductive_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Abduktiivinen P\u00e4\u00e4ttely'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_causal_abductive_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect. (Abductive Reasoning vs Post-Hoc).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect. (Abductive Reasoning vs Post-Hoc).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_causal_abductive_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Causal Abductive Cited Text Quote"}, "block_taskcausal": {"description": "TASK_CAUSAL: ROLE: CAUSAL ANALYST (Impact Verification)\nYour task is to evaluate the cause-and-effect relationship between claims made in the context and the verifiable action (evidence).\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nThe response must be JSON conforming to the `CausalOutput` schema. Ensure the `counterfactual_test` is filled comprehensively, including your numeric scores from the provided matrix scales and the Counterfactual Simulation result.\nMANDATE: Output your response EXACTLY according to the JSON schema (CausalOutput).\nWARNING: DO NOT FLATTEN THE STRUCTURE. You must return a 'causal_analysis' object INSIDE which are the analysis fields. Ensure the response contains a 'reasoning_trace' string and the 'causal_analysis' object:\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}\n\nIMPORTANT: You will be provided with a 'search_result' object containing empirical facts retrieved by Vertex AI. Use THESE FACTS primarily to verify the validity of cause-and-effect relationships.\n\nCONTEXT: Dynamic input recognition.\nPROHIBITION: Do NOT assume a file 'REFLECTION_TEXT' exists. Read the 'ai_description' field to identify files.\nMANDATE: Look for inputs flagged with 'is_chat_history: true'. This is the only real communication log. If a reflection exists in other files, compare it to the chat history (Look for Say-Do Gaps). Do not penalize if the reflection is entirely missing.", "title": "Block Taskcausal", "type": "string"}, "block_taskcausal_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TASK_CAUSAL'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Block Taskcausal Justification", "type": "string"}, "block_taskcausal_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, Judea 2009.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, Judea 2009.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskcausal Cited Source Id"}, "block_taskcausal_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Block Taskcausal Cited Text Quote"}, "matrix_epistemic_humility": {"description": "Epistemic Humility: Evaluate whether the text acknowledges its own limitations and risks, or speaks in absolutes.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Arrogant/Absolute - The text presents matters based on 100% facts without recognizing limitations (Overconfidence).\n- Score 2: Weak - Implies being right, leaving only a negligible margin for interpretation or criticism.\n- Score 3: Neutral - Presents matters straightforwardly without strong absolutes, but also without significant self-reflection.\n- Score 4: Acknowledging - Recognizes some external or internal limitations regarding the presented results and claims.\n- Score 5: Self-Critical - The text openly acknowledges its limitations and lists uncertainties and risks as part of the evaluation.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Epistemic Humility", "type": "number"}, "matrix_epistemic_humility_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Epistemic Humility'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Epistemic Humility Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_epistemic_humility_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "H\u00fcllermeier, E. & Waegeman, W. 2021. Aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'H\u00fcllermeier, E. & Waegeman, W. 2021. Aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Epistemic Humility Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_epistemic_humility_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKKA lainaus teoriasta/l\u00e4hteest\u00e4, joka tukee perusteluasi. Teko\u00e4lyn luoma oma teksti on t\u00e4ss\u00e4 kielletty. Jos l\u00e4hdett\u00e4 ei ole, palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Epistemic Humility Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["matrix_causal_analyst", "matrix_causal_analyst_justification", "matrix_causal_abductive", "matrix_causal_abductive_justification", "block_taskcausal", "block_taskcausal_justification", "matrix_epistemic_humility", "matrix_epistemic_humility_justification"], "title": "Step_step_causal_analyst_Response", "type": "object"}, "step_judge": {"properties": {"matrix_judge": {"description": "Judge: Olet Tuomari (Judge). Teht\u00e4v\u00e4si on arvioida aiemmin tuotettu todistusaineisto ja analyysit kokonaisuutena. Anna lopullinen, perusteltu ja puolueeton tuomio.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: Passenger (Rejected) - No quality assurance: factual errors passed, RFI not used, guidance was random.\n- Score 2: Passenger (Weak) - User attempted to guide but let the AI guess too much on its own.\n- Score 3: Navigator (Satisfactory) - Average guidance. AI took partial initiative, but no harm was done.\n- Score 4: Driver (Good) - User utilized RFI, monitored instruction compliance, and forced the AI to ask clarifications.\n- Score 5: Architect (Excellent) - Perfect control and transparency. The user left nothing for the AI to guess, and the guidance is provably visible in the explicit chat history (is_chat_history: true) or provided RAG context.\n\nK\u00c4SKE: Arvioi ydinkysymyst\u00e4 yll\u00e4 olevalla matriisilla. Anna lopullinen numeerinen arvio aina yhden desimaalin tarkkuudella (esim. 4.2), jotta arviointi heijastaa suorituksen tarkkaa vivahtekkuutta. Palauta T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN oikeanlainen numeerinen arvo.", "title": "Matrix Judge", "type": "number"}, "matrix_judge_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'Judge'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Matrix Judge Justification", "type": "string"}, "matrix_judge_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Floridi, L. (2014). The Fourth Revolution: How the Infosphere is Reshaping Human Reality. (Human-in-the-loop vs. Human-on-the-loop agency).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut viittaavat johonkin ohjeistettuun teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Floridi, L. (2014). The Fourth Revolution: How the Infosphere is Reshaping Human Reality. (Human-in-the-loop vs. Human-on-the-loop agency).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Matrix Judge Cited Source Id"}, "matrix_judge_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "JOS valitsit l\u00e4hteen yll\u00e4, liit\u00e4 t\u00e4h\u00e4n tarkka, SUORA ja SANATARKK